    "measurementTechnique": [
      "Water level was measured in-situ at 5 min intervals with pressure transducer loggers installed in piezometers across the marsh platform and upland (Solinst Canada Ltd., Ontario, Canada). Pore water and shallow groundwater conductivity were measured monthly using an Orion Star A329 Portable Multiparameter Meter (Thermo Scientific, Massachusetts, USA). Two 5 cm diameter sediment cores were collected at each of the three marsh positions using a Russian Peat Borer (Aquatic Research Instruments, Idaho, USA). Monthly vegetation surveys were conducted to measure canopy height, stalk length and width, and coincided with UAV surveys for NDVI measurements.\nMeteorological data from the Caspian weather station and surface water quality and tidal from the North Marsh at the Elkhorn Slough were downloaded from the NERR CDMO site (https://cdmo.baruch.sc.edu/)"
    ],
